## Props

Sets scheme, contrast, accent, shape, density, glass and look for its subtree. Providers nest, and everything inside one follows the nearest: Lede's tokens, motion set through `tokens`, high contrast, `glass="solid"` and `dark:` utilities.

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `scheme` | `'auto' \| 'inherit' \| 'light' \| 'dark'` |  | Unset inherits the nearest provider's, and is `'auto'` at the root. `'auto'` follows `prefers-color-scheme`. `'inherit'` copies the nearest provider's, or the nearest `[data-theme]` ancestor's when no provider is above. |
| `contrast` | `'auto' \| 'inherit' \| 'standard' \| 'high'` |  | Unset inherits the nearest provider's, and is `'auto'` at the root. `'auto'` follows `prefers-contrast: more`, and `'high'` selects the `-hc` theme. `'inherit'` copies the nearest provider's, or the nearest `[data-theme]` ancestor's when no provider is above. |
| `accent` | `Preset \| (string & {})` |  | A preset name, or any hex color, for which `--primary-foreground` is picked for you. Unset inherits the nearest provider's. |
| `accentForeground` | `string` |  | Text color on primary fills, for a custom accent when the automatic pick is wrong. Inherited along with `accent`. |
| `shape` | `'soft' \| 'crisp' \| 'square'` |  | Corners, from roundest to squarest. `square` has no capsules. Unset inherits the nearest provider's, or `:root`'s when no provider sets one. A provider that turns a look off (`look="lede"`) starts from Lede's corners: give it a shape of its own to keep one. |
| `density` | `'regular' \| 'compact' \| 'touch'` |  | Control heights, for buttons, fields and table hit targets. `'touch'` is for screens used with a finger: no control is shorter than `--size-hit-min`, 44px. List rows and bar items keep `--size-hit-min` in every density. Unset inherits the nearest provider's, or `:root`'s when no provider sets one. A provider that turns a look off starts from Lede's density: give it one of its own to keep one. |
| `glass` | `'regular' \| 'solid'` |  | Glass material. Unset inherits the nearest provider's, and is `'regular'` at the root. Under `prefers-reduced-transparency`, glass draws as `solid`. |
| `look` | `'lede' \| (string & {})` |  | A whole visual style over the same components, such as `'brutal'`, keyed on `data-look`: it applies once the look's CSS is on the page, from the `@lede/look-skeuo`, `@lede/look-brutal` or `@lede/look-broadsheet` registry item. It sets its own colors, corners, type, edges and depth; an accent picked here still replaces its accent, and high contrast keeps Lede's -hc palette. Unset inherits the nearest provider's. `'lede'` turns a look off, and Lede's tokens apply again inside it. |
| `surface` | `'none' \| 'base' \| 'grouped'` | `none` | The wrapper's background. Default `'none'`. |
| `tokens` | `Record<string, string>` |  | Token values by name, such as `{ radius: '18px' }`, set on the wrapper and carried into its portals. |

ThemeProvider also takes the attributes of `<div>`, such as `className`, and the `render` prop of `useRender` from `@base-ui/react/use-render`.

## Example

The smallest working use, from the docs site:

```tsx
import type { ReactNode } from 'react';
import { ThemeProvider } from '@/components/lede/theme-provider';

// Wrap the app once. A nested ThemeProvider rethemes a subtree and inherits what it leaves unset.
export function App({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) {
  return (
    <ThemeProvider surface="grouped" accent="blue">
      {children}
      <ThemeProvider scheme="dark" accent="orange">
        <p>Dark and orange, whatever the page uses.</p>
      </ThemeProvider>
    </ThemeProvider>
  );
}
```

Docs: [Components](https://lede.cloudcompute.com/components.md).

